NAME
       hexed - hex viewer and editor

SYNOPSIS
       hexed [-w] <file>

DESCRIPTION
       Shows a file as offsets, hex bytes and printable text, and edits
       it in place. It reads only the part of the file on screen, so it
       opens a whole disk as readily as a small file.

       Editing is buffered: changes are held until saved and shown
       highlighted, so what has been touched is visible before it is
       written. Writing needs -w; without it the file is opened read
       only and edits are refused.

OPTIONS
       -w     open for writing (default is read only)

KEYS
       arrows          move one byte or one line
       PgUp, PgDn      move a screen
       Home, End       start and end of the file
       Tab             switch between the hex and the text pane
       0-9 a-f         type a byte in the hex pane
       any character   type a byte in the text pane
       g               go to an offset; a leading + or - moves relative
       /               search
       n               repeat the last search
       u               undo the last change
       s               write the changes
       q               quit, asking first if anything is unsaved

SEARCHING
       A pattern is either hex bytes, with or without spaces, or text
       in double quotes. The search wraps around the end of the file
       and matches against pending edits as well as what is on disk.

EXAMPLES
       hexed /usr/share/media/giphy.gif
       hexed -w disk.img
       hexed /dev/sda

              Then / and 55aa to find a boot signature, or g and 1fe to
              jump straight to it.

SEE ALSO
       hexdump(1), dd(1), fdisk(1), curses(3)
